LOG Analyzer
============

1.) What is this tool?
2.) Usage
3.) Enhancements
4.) Disclaimer (!!!)
--------------------

1.) What is this tool?

After some crisis during production we (Logon devs) realized it is hard to get an overview on the application health.
I decided to create a tool quickly that produces some easy-on-the eye reports after parsing the application log.

Please note i checked some tools on the market but either they disliked our log pattern or simply could not load a 50 meg log file.

The log analyzer will parse all entries in the log folder (recursively) it is pointed to. WARN and ERROR entries are collected. Also it creates a report on how many expcetions happened per type. 

Testing with logs from LP0 a day of log from the 5 instances is processed in less than a minute.

2.) Usage

> python analyze_log.py /tmp/mylogfolder

There will be a folder created called 'error_report' inside that there is an index.html. 
Please open that in your browser.

3.) Enhancements

The tool could use many new features. 
But please be aware that it might effect the performance making the tool less and less useful.
It is written in python and can be extended without too much python experties

Idea: if the log pattern regexp would be a parameter it could be used for other projects as well.

4.) Disclaimer (!!!)

Although i created this tool as a personal interest i hope it will be generally useful.
PLEASE NOTE THOUGH I CREATED THE CORE IN QUASI ONE SITTING AND THE CODE QUALITY REFLECTS THAT.
It lacks some structure / design.
I already added some unit tests but many more seems to be needed for the parser.

